MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_001: A friend of mine's birthday is next month, and I\nwant to get her a gift.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_002: She reads a lot, so I thought I'd get her a book, but I\ndon't really read much, so I don't know what to buy.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_003: <NCA>Suggest buying several to be safe.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_004: <NCB>Suggest he go shopping with her.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_005: <ACA>I thought about doing that, but I'm afraid I might\ngive her something she's already read.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Kai_m01_006: <ACB>That's a great idea! I can't buy the wrong thing if\nshe's with me. Thanks! I'll try inviting her!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Kai_m01: <BLN>What should I get?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bel_m01_001: I will win any battle I enter, whether it's in the arena\nor outside it.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bel_m01_002: No matter what happens, I will survive. I will expend\nall my strength to leave this place.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Bel_m01: <BLN>Anyone I face.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dit_m01_001: Hehe... Hahaha!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dit_m01_002: House Lamine—what a fine name Esmeralda has\ngiven our clan!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dit_m01_003: Should this name reach as far as Fódlan, my sister\nmay have her own thoughts about it, however.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Dit_m01: <BLN>House Lamine!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tal_m01_001: A merchant is only as good as his business instinct.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tal_m01_002: Recognizing quality, stocking good product, and\nfiguring what the customer's truly after are key.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tal_m01_003: You need to be ahead of the curve and anticipate\nneed. That's how you get rich, you see.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Tal_m01: <BLN>Being a good merchant means...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Orh_m01_001: I must do all that I can—for Diego and the others\nhelping me with my matches!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Orh_m01_002: There's assisting with any training they need... And\nmaking snacks for when we're between sessions...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Orh_m01_003: I also have magic that I've honed during years of\nservice at the temple I work at. We'll surely win!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Orh_m01: <BLN>I'll do my very best!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Seo_m01_001: The Dagsion arena is host to no end of\nfierce matches.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Seo_m01_002: I may be queen of Saramis, but I am also a warrior.\nA well-fought battle is thrilling to behold.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Seo_m01_003: I myself fight to achieve the long-held dream of my\npeople, but it is good to know I will not grow bored.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Seo_m01: <BLN>The thrill is palpable.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Led_m01_001: The taverns here in the imperial capital are better\nfor picking up information than those in other towns.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Led_m01_002: On the downside, they seem to be better at drawing\nin hordes of men too. Ugh.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Led_m01_003: If they had something useful to say, that would be\none thing. Instead, they're all blowhards.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Led_m01: <BLN>I've picked up a lot.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Anh_m01_001: In Dagsion, water is so abundant they can use it for\nnon-essentials like decorative fountains.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Anh_m01_002: We had several wells in the village but supply was so\nlow that people treasured every drop.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Anh_m01_003: If I accomplish my mission, maybe they can know a\nlife where water is as common as it is here.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Anh_m01: <BLN>Water is common here.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tia_m01_001: I was shopping for a change of clothes when a\nshopkeeper told me my glasses looked nice.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tia_m01_002: Tee hee... It's nice to hear the things you like suit\nyou well.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Tia_m01: <BLN>I got a nice compliment...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pet_m01_001: I saw a merchant who was carrying a great big bag\nand selling all kinds of stuff. Maybe even rare stuff!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pet_m01_002: They had some really beautiful earrings I thought\nTialla might like...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pet_m01_003: I'll never be able to give them to her, though. I get\nway too embarrassed with stuff like that.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Pet_m01: <BLN>I found something she'd like, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hur_m01_001: Where did it... I... What happened to that paper?\nI need to remember what I wrote on it, and soon.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hur_m01_002: People kept jumping into the tournament, even after\nthe additional round of recruitment and now...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hur_m01_003: Ugh. Centurio's going to get so mad at me.\nWhat should I do?
MID_LGA_1_M04_Hur_m01: <BLN>What should I do?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Max_m01_001: I've got my issues, but at least I'm not greedy like\neverybody fighting in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Max_m01_002: I'm just a simple man who likes chopping people up.\nHeehee. Heh heh HEH!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Max_m01: <BLN>Heehee!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gol_m01_001: When they deck out the arena with fancy\ncontraptions, it's no wonder the crowd gets fired up.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gol_m01_002: Used to all be simpler, y'know? Stuff that popped out\nof the floor or whatever.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gol_m01_003: Or they'd surround you with fire... That's really only\nfun if you're on the watching side.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Gol_m01: <BLN>All these fancy doodads!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gat_m01_001: I hear some have died in the Heroic Games, but I\nwon't indignify them with my sympathy.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gat_m01_002: When one enters the arena, one knows death is a\npossibility. So pitying them would be an insult.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Gat_m01: <BLN>I'm not sympathetic.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dan_m01_001: It used to be I who crafted Poloni's introductory\nspeech before each match.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dan_m01_002: I must say, it impressed me, his ability to read the\nwords as if he came up with them himself.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dan_m01_003: Not that I'm bothered by it.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dan_m01_004: The master auteur is not distracted by such things.\nI do not dwell on the past, but keep writing.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Dan_m01: <BLN>I will simply keep writing.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fab_m01_001: In the five years I have roamed this land, I have\nnever tired of observing its plant life.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fab_m01_002: I delight in the mere thought of encountering new\nspecies endemic here. And sketching them.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Fab_m01: <BLN>An endless delight.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Esm_m01_001: Once I got outside my little fishing village, I\ndiscovered a whole new world of odors.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Esm_m01_002: Dagsion is full of all kinds of stink, and it all gets\nmixed up together.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Esm_m01_003: You've smelled it, right? DISGUSTING! Sometimes,\nhaving a good sense of smell isn't much fun.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Esm_m01: <BLN>Smell that!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Urs_m01_001: It seems I'm developing a reputation around the\ncompany as being...cold.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Urs_m01_002: I've always been viewed that way, even prior to\nbecoming manager.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Urs_m01_003: I'm not perfect, but I am who I am. As long as it\ndoesn't bother customers, I can live with it.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Urs_m01: <BLN>I pay it no mind.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sim_m01_001: I know a weapons dealer who says he's making a\nkilling off the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sim_m01_002: With Solel willing to grant any wish, folks are paying\ntop coin for anything that'll help them win.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sim_m01_003: They think they're going to beat the odds and make\nit rich. Heh! Not if I have anything to say about it.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Sim_m01: <BLN>There's this guy I know...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_001: Hey, I could really use your advice...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_002: I probably shouldn't bother you with this, but I could\nreally use some advice...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_003: Let's say you like someone, but they have some\npretty gross red flags...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_004: Let's say you have feelings for someone, but they\nhave some pretty gross red flags...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_005: Should you just accept that person's flaws? Or should\nyou hold out hope that they'll change?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_006: Should you just accept that person's flaws? Or should\nyou hold out hope that they'll change?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_007: <NCA>Tell her to accept the person's faults.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_008: <NCB>Tell her to ask the person to change.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_009: <ACA>Yeah, you're right. Talimun would probably say the\nsame thing... OH! But—this isn't about him, OK?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_010: <ACA>Yeah, you're right. Talimun would probably say the\nsame thing... OH! But—this isn't about him, OK?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_011: <ACB>But this person's lived for hundreds of years without\ncleaning up after himself. It probably wouldn't work...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lou_m01_012: <ACB>But this person's lived for hundreds of years without\ncleaning up after himself. It probably wouldn't work...
MID_LGA_1_M04_Lou_m01: <BLN>Can I ask your advice?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fia_m01_001: I lived in Dagsion for years after Centurio saved me.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fia_m01_002: I never got accustomed to the crowds, though.\nWould that I could spend my days in silence.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Fia_m01_003: Then again, I doubt my memory will return if I\ncommit to comfort. I must persevere...
MID_LGA_1_M04_Fia_m01: <BLN>For my memory...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Die_m01_001: If Credna isn't here, I don't think I'll have much to\ndo for the temple.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Die_m01_002: I often deliver items and messages to places far from\nthe temple. Simple work for a forest warrior.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Die_m01_003: Lots of people give me a dirty look when they learn\nthat I'm from a forest clan. Yeah, I don't care.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Die_m01: <BLN>I'll kill time, I guess.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lor_m01_001: Watching the gods at the big ceremony made me\nthink...they're all kinda sparkly in an intense way.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lor_m01_002: Credna was the first god I met. So I wondered if\nthey were all more like him.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lor_m01_003: He's more kinda easygoing than intense and\nsparkly. Easier to spend time with.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Lor_m01: <BLN>So, Credna is more like...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Set_m01_001: I realized something when I was fishing the other\nday and stared at my reflection in the water.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Set_m01_002: I only dyed my hair for the sake of my mission.\nBut I actually quite like it!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Set_m01: <BLN>My hair color...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Nin_m01_001: With the Heroic Games underway, the imperial\ncity is growing more and more crowded.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Nin_m01_002: I've been in Dagsion for a long time. I've never seen\ncrowds like this... Never in all my time here.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Nin_m01_003: I find myself lost in a strange fog when around so\nmany people. I prefer the quiet of the temples.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Nin_m01: <BLN>Like being lost in a fog...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bon_m01_001: Children of Damascar live in harmony with nature,\nwhich is why they are called the forest peoples.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bon_m01_002: But beyond that, we are also skilled sailors. The sea\nis our ally as we read the currents and stars.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Bon_m01_003: We are proud that our skill surpasses any in the\nempire...but it may be wise to keep that quiet.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Bon_m01: <BLN>We are more than we seem.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tob_m01_001: I thought the Heroic Games would go all day and\nnight, but there's a lotta downtime.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tob_m01_002: Dunno why. Maybe the festival part is more\nimportant to the higher-ups than the matches.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Tob_m01_003: Well, it sure makes the capital an interesting place.\nNever a dull moment here!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Tob_m01: <BLN>Who'd have thought?
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lil_m01_001: I noticed lots of the women here are decked out in\npretty fancy outfits.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lil_m01_002: But I prefer to wear stuff you can move in. It's better\nfor fighting and moving through the forest.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lil_m01_003: Although when I was little, my parents would also\ndress me in those same fancy clothes...
MID_LGA_1_M04_Lil_m01: <BLN>The frilly stuff's not for me.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lys_m01_001: Gambling on the matches seems like a popular\npastime here. It's not to my taste, though.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lys_m01_002: But I can see how it might add to the excitement of\nthe games, so I'll try to keep an open mind about it.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Lys_m01: <BLN>I'll try to withhold judgment.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Buc_m01_001: With only a few days before the match, I must\nprepare to best protect milady.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Buc_m01_002: I'll put even more effort into my training. Perhaps I'll\nstart with a thousand more practice swings.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Buc_m01: <BLN>I must protect milady.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_001: My many talents include composing poetry,\ndancing, and playing beautiful melodies.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_002: Some might wrongheadedly attribute this to my\nexposure to the arts since youth.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_003: Nay, I have simply been superior all along.\nMy gifts are god-given.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him his talent comes from hard work.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_005: <NCB>Warn him there could be trouble if he's negligent.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_006: <ACA>While I appreciate the compliment, it would be\ntactless to boast of my own efforts!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_007: <ACA>My devotion to Kalla, goddess of the arts, dictates\nthat I must credit her for my talents.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_008: <ACA>You honor me with such a remark. However,\nit would be tactless of me to flaunt my own efforts.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_009: <ACA>My devotion to Kalla, goddess of the arts, dictates\nthat I must credit her for my talents.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_010: <ACB>Ahaha, and that would only invigorate my passion\nfor the arts!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sci_m01_011: <ACB>Ahaha, and that would only invigorate my passion\nfor the arts!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Sci_m01: <BLN>My talent is god-given.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Moo_m01_001: There are lots of men in the imperial capital.\nGotta keep a watch out!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Moo_m01_002: You know, men like Sirocco, who won't stop chasing\nwomen. Who have pretty faces, and are strong...
MID_LGA_1_M04_Moo_m01: <BLN>I have to be wary.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Mic_m01_001: When it comes to magic, Smyrnos is number one\nin Dagda, both in knowledge and power.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Mic_m01_002: From the sound of it, he's breaking new ground in\nmagic just about every day.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Mic_m01_003: I'd like to make his acquaintance, for my daughter's\nsake, but I don't have the money...
MID_LGA_1_M04_Mic_m01: <BLN>You should know this.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Oly_m01_001: You can tell the Heroic Games are a grand event by\nhow many gods are here to attend them!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Oly_m01_002: Knowing that they'll be watching us makes me all\nthe more motivated.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Oly_m01_003: Indeed, I'll put in such a gorgeous performance that\neven those not in attendance catch word of it!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Oly_m01: <BLN>Yes, it motivates me!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_001: Last time I went to the training grounds, I started by\npracticing my breathing techniques, same as always.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_002: There's a guy there who starts telling me it's a waste\nof time, and how breathing doesn't build muscle.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_003: Like I'm gonna listen to what a stranger thinks.\nThis is how I learned to train!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_004: <NCA>Agree he should do things his way.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_005: <NCB>Advise him to keep an open mind.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_006: <ACA>Right?! If they think some other way would be better,\nthen that's how they should train!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Naz_m01_007: <ACB>Sometimes, maybe. But I bet it'd bug you too if a\nrandom guy told you you're training wrong!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Naz_m01: <BLN>This is how I do things!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sar_m01_001: I knew we would see lots of people once we left\nthe village.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sar_m01_002: There are good people to be found, but lots of bad\nas well. Why aren't they caught and arrested?
MID_LGA_1_M04_Sar_m01: <BLN>They should be arrested.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dai_m01_001: There's all kinds of new food to try now that we're\nout of the village. Meat, fish, veggies...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dai_m01_002: No matter where ya go, there's nothing but good\nsmells! I'm always hungry.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Dai_m01_003: It makes me mad that people with money can eat all\nthey want, when they want!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Dai_m01: <BLN>I smell food!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hal_m01_001: Bridal Party of the Pale Raven is such a cool name\nfor Anatolia's clan.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hal_m01_002: And the spectators seem to like it. I'm kinda proud\nof myself for coming up with such a great name!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Hal_m01_003: Oh...but what if we become famous because of it?\nWould that be bad?! I don't know!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Hal_m01: <BLN>Such a cool name.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Guj_m01_001: I'm legendary, if you haven't heard! I'd write a book\nseries about my life, but I'd die before I could finish.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Guj_m01_002: But if I was able to finish one volume of it...it'd sell\nlike mad and I'd be the richest man in Dagda!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Guj_m01_003: And then my massive fortune would surely start a\nmajor war.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Guj_m01: <BLN>It'd start a war!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Yan_m01_001: The likes of gods are never to be relied on. We all\nshould achieve our wishes by our own hand.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Yan_m01_002: But I can't deny the visceral thrill of watching heroes\nclash, putting body and soul at stake.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Yan_m01_003: The Heroic Games—such a compromising event on\nvarious levels!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Yan_m01: <BLN>These Heroic Games...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Iio_m01_001: I can't believe he's still alive, or that such a man has\ncome to be called the White-Maned Demon.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Iio_m01_002: I'd know his fighting style anywhere, but as to the\nman's character...it's growing unrecognizable.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Iio_m01_003: Some time ago, I witnessed his conduct in a\nmock battle and was highly impressed.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Iio_m01: <BLN>I'd know his technique anywhere.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pep_m01_001: We ourselves had thought it impossible to feast upon\ntrue seafood here, given that Dagsion is on a lake.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pep_m01_002: But we are impressed to find that fish caught the\nworld over is shipped to this capital.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Pep_m01_003: As made here, in basic ways for common appetites,\nseafood dishes lack panache but still intrigue!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Pep_m01: <BLN>The flavors lack panache, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Noc_m01_001: Something great is going to happen to you! It just\nstruck me...like being hit by lightning!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Noc_m01_002: It's clear as day now, so it's a sure thing.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Noc_m01_003: You're going to win your next match! Oh! And\nanother great thing...happens after that!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Noc_m01: <BLN>I see good things for you!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sop_m01_001: Anna works for the temple, same as I do, though\nshe's essential in running the entire Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sop_m01_002: I should treat her to dinner to show my\nappreciation. Tasty food is great for morale.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Sop_m01_003: Ah, that's right... The last time I tried to treat her,\nAnna ended up treating me! What a pickle.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Sop_m01: <BLN>I appreciate her so much.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cat_m01_001: So Suarez made his way to Dagsion too. We're from\nthe same county. I'd have liked to speak with him.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cat_m01_002: But, deceased is deceased. That door is closed. It's a\nshame, but his death made a statement of sorts.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cat_m01_003: People can say what they like, but one thing is\ncertain—he died on his own terms.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Cat_m01: <BLN>I had no idea...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ned_m01_001: Being a good mercenary is more than just fighting\nwell. It's taking time to provide guidance too.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ned_m01_002: Right before the Heroic Games began, a lot of\nnewcomers to battle were asking me for instruction.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ned_m01_003: But really, I couldn't condone that—hasty training to\nhelp get them into the competition. Unbelievable!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Ned_m01: <BLN>Truly unbelievable...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Zac_m01_001: The Heroic Games are bringin' all sorts here to\nthe city. From all over!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Zac_m01_002: Easy enough to yoink money off anyone who's\nnot payin' attention. Heh heh!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Zac_m01: <BLN>Time to go fishin'!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Maj_m01_001: I hate gladiators! Every time I bet on one, they\ngo and lose my money!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Maj_m01_002: My whole stash, just flushed into the gutter! What\nthe hell already!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Maj_m01: <BLN>Damn gladiators!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ven_m01_001: These would-be soldiers! They wouldn't have even\napproached competence without me!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ven_m01_002: Now they have the GALL to refuse me as their\nleader for the next match?!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Ven_m01_003: Honestly, they better not come groveling when I get\nmy territory to rule over. Idiots!
MID_LGA_1_M04_Ven_m01: <BLN>Wretched fools!
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cen_m01_001: The old fool's always giving me unsolicited advice.\n"Try having a family before you die," he says. Heh.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Cen_m01_002: I understand the appeal of a family, but my duty will\nalways come first.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Cen_m01: <BLN>He thinks he knows it all...
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gab_m01_001: I expected a lot of folks to participate in the games.\nWhat surprises me is the number of wounded. 
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gab_m01_002: Might have to get ahold of more bandages before\nwe run out.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Gab_m01_003: Maybe I'll send someone around the Port of Pandora\nto top up our supply.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Gab_m01: <BLN>I'm tellin' ya.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lin_m01_001: For some reason, this place has seen more\nvisitors lately.
MID_LGV_1_M04_Lin_m01_002: Well, I don't want any. I'm not anyone's sideshow.
MID_LGA_1_M04_Lin_m01: <BLN>Leave me in peace.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B01_m01_001: Whew. Finally made it through customs. It takes\nforever for them to inspect all the cargo.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B01_m01_002: Some palms can be greased, but doing it for\neverything can really hurt the bottom line.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B01_m01: <BLN>That took forever...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B02_m01_001: The thin, specially shaped glass used for spectacles\nisn't easy to make, even for a skilled artisan.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B02_m01_002: I know that, and I still wish my apprentice would\nshow faster progress. I won't be around forever.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B02_m01_003: Well, these things take time. I'll just have to continue\nmentoring him for a few more years.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B02_m01: <BLN>This requires a delicate technique.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B03_m01_001: Do wild ornius eggs taste good? I want to find out.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B03_m01_002: I've always had a hankering for wild cuisine. And I\ndon't know any hunters, so the craving's real bad.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B03_m01: <BLN>How would they taste?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B04_m01_001: That match with Forgotten Alcor was terrible,\nI tell you!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B04_m01_002: I fear to see such barbarism in a sacred battle meant\nas an offering to Dagda the Great.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B04_m01: <BLN>Gods preserve us...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B05_m01_001: Jurah is the goddess of abundance and cultivation.\nShe's the one us farmers revere.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B05_m01_002: And she doesn't get out too much, so I was moved to\nsee her in the luxury seats.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B05_m01: <BLN>A rare sighting indeed!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B06_m01_001: A new soothsayer in town is getting attention, but I\nsay she's disrespecting Fortuna, the Goddess of Fate.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B06_m01_002: Though I'm a little curious as to her methods...maybe\nI should try it once to observe. Nothing more.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B06_m01: <BLN>Such dreadful disrespect.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B07_m01_001: I got scolded for fumbling my sacred magic a bit.\nIt's harder than it looks!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B07_m01_002: But there's no shortage of injuries during the Heroic\nGames, so I'll have plenty of chances to practice.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B07_m01: <BLN>I just need to practice...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B08_m01_001: Did the prophet Jehoshaphat truly know what the\nfuture held?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B08_m01_002: Honestly, I don't believe it, but some folks in this\nworld do have mysterious powers.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B08_m01: <BLN>Was the prophet real?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B09_m01_001: I know it's my job, but it's such a hassle dealing with\nall these drunks.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B09_m01_002: Smiling and nodding at their bragging, clearing up\ntheir vomit...both happen more often than I'd like.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B09_m01: <BLN>I didn't sign up for this.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B10_m01_001: I used a branch that fell from a tree and a rock I\nfound to make a kinda spear-type thing.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B10_m01_002: Once I find a cloth to wrap around my neck, I can\nplay soldier with everyone!
MID_LGA_1_M04_B10_m01: <BLN>OK, now I'm gonna...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B11_m01_001: I won't have a Saramis soldier as an ally. I value\ncoming back from the battlefield alive, you see.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B11_m01_002: So no, I won't be fighting alongside someone who\nprays to the Keeper of Death and Night.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B11_m01: <BLN>Those weirdos from Saramis...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B12_m01_001: Only my experience with spirit magic got these old\nbones to the imperial capital.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B12_m01_002: I can drive off any common bandit, or beast of\nreasonable size, without a problem.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B12_m01_003: Wisdom and learning won't let you down, even as\nyour body declines.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B12_m01: <BLN>Don't count me out just yet.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B13_m01_001: Ugh, still no sign of the ship. It was scheduled to\nhave made it to port last month.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B13_m01_002: Well, I can just relax and sip coffee while I wait.\nI get paid either way, so no skin off my nose.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B13_m01: <BLN>The ship's still not here!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B14_m01_001: Gotta say, Saraminian ships are a cut above.\nOur own run-down buckets don't compare.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B14_m01_002: I take extra pains not to bump into 'em. Wouldn't\nwant to get into it with the children of Damascar.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B14_m01: <BLN>Those Saraminian ships...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B15_m01_001: I can't get over the intriguing taste of the candy I\nhad when I was down south recently.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B15_m01_002: It smelled as good as it tasted. I think they thicken\nit with fermented obroma seeds.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B15_m01: <BLN>What was it called again?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B16_m01_001: I've been doing the rounds here for a while, but there\ndoesn't seem to be any risk of serious trouble.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B16_m01_002: That's because the ships berthed here have their\ncargo checked at Forts Hecatoncheires and Galcar.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B16_m01: <BLN>You can't be too careful.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B17_m01_001: What's really going on between King Gilchris and\nChancellor Martila?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B17_m01_002: The chancellor seems strangely close to the king,\nconsidering she was his father's second wife.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B17_m01: <BLN>I wouldn't ask this too loud, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B18_m01_001: If only I could find a new magic tutor! All mine does\nis lecture me on the theory.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B18_m01_002: But nobody pays me any mind when I complain.\nMaybe I should just run away from home.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B18_m01: <BLN>This is intolerable!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B19_m01_001: As the viceroy's son, I thought making an appearance\nat the games would be tiresome.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B19_m01_002: But these gladiatorial matches are more exciting than\nI anticipated. I find myself quite enjoying them.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B19_m01_003: Out in the countryside, the only bloodsport we get\nis going on a hunt.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B19_m01: <BLN>Despite myself, it's fascinating.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B20_m01_001: There's a strange story about the temple of Aurora\nhere. Have you heard it yet?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B20_m01_002: Visiting worshippers have vanished into thin air\nwithout any rhyme or reason.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B20_m01_003: You should be careful setting foot in the place.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B20_m01: <BLN>Be very careful...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B21_m01_001: Most folks misunderstand this, but the Lake Baal\nthat surrounds Dagsion is not the ocean.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B21_m01_002: Though it's so vast that I can see where the\nconfusion comes from.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B21_m01: <BLN>It's a common misconception.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B22_m01_001: The number of merchants who can undertake trade\nwith Fódlan is rather limited.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B22_m01_002: Naturally, the Vandahl Trading Company can do it.\nThey're among the largest merchants in Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B22_m01_003: If you're looking for them, their Dagsion branch is\nnear the port.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B22_m01: <BLN>Vandahl doesn't think small.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B23_m01_001: Some guy called Majide who was set to enter the\nHeroic Games picked a fight just before the match.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B23_m01_002: Bad idea, because it seems to have cost Majide his\nright to enter the games.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B23_m01: <BLN>It's the talk of the town...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B24_m01_001: I wanted to visit Fortuna's temple, but I've been up\nand down Temple Row and can't find the entrance.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B24_m01_002: It seems weird that there'd be a temple you can't get\nto from Temple Row...
MID_LGA_1_M04_B24_m01: <BLN>That's strange...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B25_m01_001: There's no way the White-Maned Demon lost...\nI can't remember that happening before.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B25_m01_002: Who even is this Cruaidín, anyway? I've never\nheard of the guy!
MID_LGA_1_M04_B25_m01: <BLN>What an upset!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B26_m01_001: Do you know about this flamma stuff? Some folks\ncall it Droplets of Dawn.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B26_m01_002: Like the name says, it's a liquid that glows the color\nof the sky at daybreak.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B26_m01_003: But that's as much as I know. No idea where I can\nget my hands on some.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B26_m01: <BLN>I'd like to pick some up, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B27_m01_001: There's been a spate of mysterious assaults around\nDagsion recently.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B27_m01_002: Oddly, the victims are all well-known fighters.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B27_m01_003: We don't have any leads on a suspect, but whoever\nit is, they must be a fearsome combatant.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B27_m01_004: If you ask me, there ought to be a curfew imposed\nuntil this case is resolved.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B27_m01: <BLN>It's a public safety risk.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B28_m01_001: Owing to the rash of assaults, there's an increased\nguard presence at the temples.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B28_m01_002: Whoever's behind them isn't afraid to target Heroic\nGames participants, after all.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B28_m01_003: Unless they mobilize the vulkans, I worry we're only\ngoing to see more victims over time.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B28_m01: <BLN>Not to sound like a coward, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B29_m01_001: The colosseum was completed about 450 years ago,\nsomewhere around the year 1000.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B29_m01_002: It's the centerpiece of the whole plaza.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B29_m01_003: Which makes me wonder...what was here before\nthey built the colosseum?
MID_LGA_1_M04_B29_m01: <BLN>It's a splendid colosseum, isn't it?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B30_m01_001: Tarvos is a desert region to the west of Dagsion.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B30_m01_002: I hear it was grassland once upon a time, but it's\na wasteland now. I'd steer clear if I were you.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B30_m01: <BLN>Tarvos isn't pretty...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B31_m01_001: The Battle of Tarvos was a major conflict in ancient\ntimes, before the Dagdan Empire was founded.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B31_m01_002: It was the final battle between Iskandariya\nand the Dagdan pantheon.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B31_m01_003: Not many records of that time remain, but it was\nsaid to be a bitter struggle.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B31_m01: <BLN>Not many details survived.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B32_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B32_m01_001: The young king and queen of Arago are among the\nstate visitors invited to view the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B32_m01_002: I got to see them for myself. The queen is absolutely\ngorgeous in person!
MID_LGV_1_M04_B32_m01_003: But the king came off as a little cruel. Though maybe\nit was just nerves.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B32_m01: <BLN>It was only a passing glance, but...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B33_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B33_m01_001: Did you notice that of all the Dagdan pantheon, only\nFortuna's temple has no entrance on Temple Row?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B33_m01_002: The truth is that her temple was built even farther\nback, out behind Dagda's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B33_m01_003: But no one knows for sure why they put it there.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B33_m01: <BLN>It's a mystery...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B34_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B34_m01_001: The empire's control doesn't extend to Southern\nDagda, which is crawling with barbarians.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B34_m01_002: Some of them are the Mosa, a force who've tried\ntime and again to invade Northern Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B34_m01_003: But Saramis has always driven them back at the\nsouthernmost point of Northern Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B34_m01_004: That's why the kingdom of Saramis is nicknamed\n"the Shield of Dagda."
MID_LGA_1_M04_B34_m01: <BLN>It's a land of barbarians...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B35_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B35_m01_001: Credna and Kalla are siblings, born from Dagda\nthe Great and Jurah.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B35_m01_002: Lord Solel and Mars have a lot of affection for Jurah.\nThey see her as a role model of sorts.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B35_m01_003: Jurah is happy to play the part for them. It's rather\nheartwarming.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B35_m01: <BLN>The whole family gets along well.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B36_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B36_m01_001: There is a set of powerful magical items crafted by\nthe gods, which we know as Arcs.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B36_m01_002: They may take the form of weapons, shields, masks,\nrings, or what have you.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B36_m01_003: Even a few books of powerful spells are counted\namong them.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B36_m01: <BLN>Truly, they are tools of the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B37_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B37_m01_001: Huh...it just occurred to me...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B37_m01_002: Wouldn't we be less conspicuous if we didn't have\nsomeone standing guard?
MID_LGV_1_M04_B37_m01_003: Hey! Get outta here! You're trespassing.
MID_LGA_1_M04_B37_m01: <BLN>Huh...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B38_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M04_B38_m01_001: Our deity is busy with his research and thus unable\nto grant audiences for the moment.
MID_LGV_1_M04_B38_m01_002: Making time to listen to the pleas of the people is an\nimportant responsibility of the gods, and yet...
MID_LGV_1_M04_B38_m01_003: Smyrnos has become fixated on these strange\nautomata of his. What am I to do with him?
MID_LGA_1_M04_B38_m01: <BLN>What am I to do with him?